  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Draws a line from (line_x0,line_y0) to (line_x1,line_y1) with the brush: sets point_routine to $17ad, then draw_line."},
    {"at":11,"placement":"line","text":"Draws a line from (line_x0,line_y0) to (line_x1,line_y1) with inverted pixels: sets point_routine to $18c2 (XOR plot, with the mirror points when mirror_mode is set), then draw_line."},
    {"at":22,"placement":"line","text":"Draws a line from (line_x0,line_y0) to (line_x1,line_y1) with the routine at point_routine (Bresenham). A vertical or horizontal line plots both end points. Another line plots line_dx or line_dy points: not the end point. Keeps $3e-$41. Changes A, X, Y, cursor_x, cursor_y."},
    {"at":40,"placement":"line","text":"A line that is not vertical and not horizontal: keeps $3e-$41 on the stack and gets the distances and directions."},
    {"at":124,"placement":"line","text":"Gets $3e-$41 back from the stack and returns."},
    {"at":137,"placement":"line","text":"Plots the point (X,Y) with the routine at point_routine. $18f7 gives the bitmap address of the point."},
    {"at":137,"placement":"side","text":"This load has no effect: $18f7 loads A from Y first."},
    {"at":146,"placement":"line","text":"Inverts the pixel at (cursor_x,cursor_y) and at the 3 mirror points (159-x,y), (159-x,199-y) and (x,199-y). Keeps cursor_x and cursor_y."},
    {"at":159,"placement":"side","text":"Mirror point on X: 159 - x."},
    {"at":173,"placement":"side","text":"Mirror point on Y: 199 - y."},
    {"at":205,"placement":"line","text":"Inverts the pixel at (X,Y): gets the bitmap address ($18f7), then $18ca."},
    {"at":211,"placement":"line","text":"Horizontal line: sorts the X values, then plots each point from line_x0 to line_x1. Keeps line_x0 and line_x1."},
    {"at":256,"placement":"line","text":"Vertical line: sorts the Y values, then plots each point from line_y0 to line_y1. Keeps line_y0 and line_y1."},
    {"at":301,"placement":"line","text":"Line with line_dx > line_dy: line_two_dy = 2*dy, line_two_dx = -2*dx, line_error = 2*dy - dx. Plots line_dx points."},
    {"at":430,"placement":"line","text":"Step on Y. When line_fill_corners is set, it first plots the corner point (new X, old Y)."},
    {"at":471,"placement":"line","text":"Line with line_dy >= line_dx: line_two_dx = 2*dx, line_two_dy = -2*dy, line_error = 2*dx - dy. Plots line_dy points."},
    {"at":600,"placement":"line","text":"Step on X. When line_fill_corners is set, it first plots the corner point (old X, new Y)."}
  ],
